{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyG3tkRyUr9K7bYAGutd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan\n\n1. **Do not wire the blocking pre-commit hook yet.** The baseline is red — the check would immediately block all work (including unrelated edits) on its first firing, making it a footgun that gets deleted, not fixed.\n\n2. **Fix the coupling mismatch first.** Determine which source is correct (pricing tier or docs), reconcile them, and land that fix to main. Verify `npm run check:pricing-sync` passes.\n\n3. **Run the check at baseline (green) in CI.** Add it to the CI pipeline running against the repaired state so it stays green and proves the check is reliable before it may block.\n\n4. **Then wire the pre-commit hook as blocking.** Once the check runs green in CI at baseline and contributors see it working in their local workflow, arm it as a blocking gate. It will now catch *future* mismatches without false-positive blocking of unrelated work.\n\n---\n\n**Hook status:** ❌ **Do not arm yet.** The baseline is disclosed-red; blocking now violates the governing rule and will paralyze the team."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":250,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
